### This script was written by a human and optimized using Claude LLM
### Modified: (1) jaccard_tree_dist returns c(distance, a, b, c) so the
### symmetric-difference distance (b + c) is derived from the SAME call
### without recomputing degree3_split_names twice; (2) added Trfbs_a/b/c
### AND (this revision) srfbs_a/b/c, sqrfbs_a/b/c, mrfbs_a/b/c -- the
### bootstrap-averaged a/b/c for every comparison, not just the true-network
### one -- bringing the matrix to 20x33; (3) both the Jaccard-normalized
### matrices (MM3/MM4) and symmetric matrices (MM32/MM42) are computed
### and saved. (4) NEW: appended genuine average-of-ratios precision/
### recall/F1/normalized-symmetric-diff columns (computed per bootstrap
### tree, then averaged, rather than derived from the already-averaged
### a/b/c totals) for each of the 4 identities (True, S, SQ, M),
### bringing the matrix to 20x49.
library(ape)
